course: dictionary
lesson: 152
title: Affordable and what it means
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Affordable means cheap enough for people to be able to buy or pay for. Afford means to have enough money to pay for something, so if you can afford it, it is affordable.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Affordable housing» is about homes, and «affordable prices» is about how much things cost. In both, the clue is money: can ordinary people pay for it?
explain: Use the comparison forms to compare prices. Affordable, more affordable and most affordable show how the cost of things compares. If one bag is more affordable than another, it costs less.
explain: In the news, «The Affordable Care Act, often called Obamacare, became law in 2010; it made insurers cover people who were already ill, with a pre-existing condition, and helped many more people get insured.» The name tells you the health cover was meant to be something people could pay for.
fact: Affordable means cheap enough for people to be able to buy or pay for.
fact: Afford means to have enough money to pay for something.
fact: «Affordable housing» means homes that people on ordinary incomes can pay for.
fact: Affordable, more affordable and most affordable compare how easy something is to pay for.
fact: Check your meaning by swapping in "cheap enough to pay for" and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: Mum says the new bike is affordable. What does she mean? | It is the biggest bike in the shop | *It costs little enough that we can pay for it | It can fly | It is very old and rusty
exercise: The council plans «affordable housing» for families. What does this mean? | *Homes that families can pay for | Homes that are empty and locked | Homes only for the very rich | Homes made of gold
exercise: Three bags cost £5, £8 and £12. Which bag is the most affordable? | *The £5 bag | The £12 bag | The £8 bag
test: What does affordable mean in «The Affordable Care Act»? | Free for ever, with nothing to pay | *Cover that people can pay for | A law about cars | Only for people who are never ill
test: Which sentence uses affordable correctly? | Affordable runs very fast across the field | *The school trip is affordable, so every child can go | The moon is affordable at night
exam: Which answer best explains what affordable means? | It means always free | *It means cheap enough for people to be able to pay for it | It means the price is high enough to be a treat | It means the thing is broken
